+# FAA subpoena follow-up in handwritten notes and a second receiving-file copy
+
+November 9, 2026 Eastern · B129 / PD04 / PD07. Three exact members of the public Commission archive add a handwritten reference to reviewing the effectiveness of a subpoena, a second filing context for the December tape request, and a January packet of proposed aviation-security questions. The corrected May 2003 answer and the later administrative disposition remain separate acquisition targets. [National Archives series descriptions](https://www.archives.gov/research/9-11/commission-series.html) · [Public Commission archive package](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NARA_9-11_Commission_Records_Released_Jan_14_2009.zip)
+
+## The November request and minutes approval
+
+- **Kaplan item 247, physical p. 33, bottom two entries.** The handwritten observations are read as **“TK REPORT”** and **“TR review - effectiveness of 1st sub”**, with **“sub”** underlined. Keep the initials and abbreviation as recorded. The same page contains discussion of a DOD notice and announcement. The draft November 6–7 minutes, item 248 p. 13 lines 16–17, explicitly identify the FAA subpoena, attribute the request to Commissioner Roemer and record the General Counsel’s offer to reply. The December meeting packet p. 15 preserves the typed passage in its minutes copy. These are records of discussion and an offer. The actual reply, report and delivery remain unlocated. [Earlier acquisition and typed passage](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/03ecaa88fa94ac032aeee7ec193a850d0983b1d5/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-subpoena-compliance-minutes-2026-11-09/README.md) · [Commission finding aid](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/finding-aid.pdf)
+- **Kaplan item 247, physical p. 3, lower entry.** The handwritten note reads **“minutes approved”**. The November agenda p. 1 lines 16–18 lists the September 23 and October 14 minutes. The November draft p. 2 lines 14–15 and the December packet's November minutes p. 4 lines 19–20 both record approval of those two meetings’ minutes. The December packet approval sentence was checked on the page image. This adds a contemporaneous approval account beside the agenda. The exact approved text, whether it incorporated the handwritten changes, and approval of the November 6–7 minutes themselves remain separate questions. [Prior packets and approval agenda](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/03ecaa88fa94ac032aeee7ec193a850d0983b1d5/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-subpoena-compliance-minutes-2026-11-09/README.md)
+
+## The December 22 request in two files
+
+Dunne item **404** in the Commission’s DOT correspondence folder and the held Marcus item **281** in the FAA folder contain closely matching copies of the three-page December 22 letter and attachment. The letter reports discovery of unproduced tapes through field-office interviews and distinguishes the attachment from the wider subpoena obligation. The attachment calls for additional tapes and records the Commission’s different descriptions of Cleveland’s four-hour blocks and Indianapolis’s excerpts. Preserve those as the Commission’s observations at that point. The two scans supply two filing contexts for the same request. An FAA receipt or fulfillment record is still needed. [Prior Marcus copy and scope](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/8852fec54eb6e8e0507a75e4cd3463a3f4430154/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-july18-receiving-file-2026-11-08/README.md) · [Archive package](https://archive.org/download/911datasets/NARA_9-11_Commission_Records_Released_Jan_14_2009.zip)
+
+| Attachment observation, physical p. 3 | Marcus 281 | Dunne 404 |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Embedded sorted text, line 6 | `ZNY, ZBW, ZDC, ZIB & ZOB` | `ZNY, ZBW, ZDC, Zffi & ZOB` |
+| Selected page-image crop | `ZNY, ZBW, ZDC, ZIB & ZOB` | `ZNY, ZBW, ZDC, ZIB & ZOB` |
+
+The source layers and archive copies are retained separately. The image observations agree at the selected field. The extracted value still differs, the file and page-raster hashes differ, and only page 2's complete extracted text matches after joining layout whitespace. No standard facility code was substituted. A native attachment or certified legible counterpart would be useful for downstream field matching. [Sources and reading coordinates](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## The January question packet
+
+**Team 7 item 378, physical p. 1 lines 7, 10, 12 and 14–53, p. 2 lines 4–17.** The January 16, 2004 email printout proposes questions under the headings **“Garvey and Flynn:”** and **“Garvey:”**. Topics include Logan screening, red-team testing, guidance on box cutters, CAPPS and prior warnings. Its subject shows **“Roehmer's”** on the image, while the archive filename has **“Roemer”**. Keep both labels. The packet records proposed questions. The addressee’s receipt, use at a hearing or interview, and the underlying warning documents and answers are open. The body supplies no completed November FAA subpoena assessment. The sender field remains redacted and is outside this comparison. [Commission finding aid](https://www.archives.gov/files/research/9-11/finding-aid.pdf) · [Exact item and hash](SOURCE-PINS.json)
+
+## Verification and outstanding records
+
+Rechecked seven SHA-256 values and ZIP CRCs, 28 embedded-text anchors, and the text and raster equality flags for the two December copies. Acquired 46 new physical pages. Checked a low-resolution page index of all 41 Kaplan pages and read 15 selected pages at larger scale. The handwritten readings above are scoped to two passages. The complete manuscript was preserved without claiming a full transcription. Scanned facility and subject readings are separate from the automated checks.
+
+- **PD04 / PD07.** Seek the actual reply or briefing to Roemer, the Commission's approved-minute version or edit/approval record, and the signed FAA return, tape manifest and Commission intake keyed to the December attachment. The two filing copies do not count as two separate transmissions.
+- **PD01–PD03.** The corrected answer to the May 2003 question, dated acknowledgment, signed action/no-action decision and case-specific recommendation responses, implementation and closure remain unacquired. The January questions and the tape-production records establish separate research leads. [Open records queue](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/055ef54a857b46846d0038109bab7e108970f03a/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-postreport-disposition-2026-10-27/OPEN-RECORDS.md)
